%YAML 1.1
%TAG !u! tag:unity3d.com,2011:
--- !u!114 &11400000
MonoBehaviour:
  m_ObjectHideFlags: 0
  m_CorrespondingSourceObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabInstance: {fileID: 0}
  m_PrefabAsset: {fileID: 0}
  m_GameObject: {fileID: 0}
  m_Enabled: 1
  m_EditorHideFlags: 0
  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: cbaf4aa92205ea54c8238e99b1f42bb3, type: 3}
  m_Name: 
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: HumanEye.Runtime::HumanEye.DialogueDatabase
  cues:
  - id: S02_L01
    scene: Scene02
    speaker: Niko
    type: Core
    layer: StoryboardCore
    text: "Hey! I\u2019m Niko. Your Vision Investigator Officer."
    filename: 01_hey_im_niko_your
    visualCue: Niko materialises and waves; medium shot
    completionEvent: audio_complete
    sequence: 1
    segments:
    - "Hey! I\u2019m Niko. Your Vision Investigator Officer."
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 458d19e8d3deee0448d11dacfd8a90e0, type: 3}
  - id: S02_L02
    scene: Scene02
    speaker: Niko
    type: Core
    layer: StoryboardCore
    text: So you want to know how light becomes sight?
    filename: 02_so_you_want_to
    visualCue: Niko gestures toward the starlight beam
    completionEvent: audio_complete
    sequence: 2
    segments:
    - So you want to know how light becomes sight?
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 2265320aa6e47394aac853654dea305b, type: 3}
  - id: S02_L03
    scene: Scene02
    speaker: Niko
    type: Core
    layer: StoryboardCore
    text: Then watching from out here won't help.
    filename: 03_then_watching_from_out
    visualCue: Niko turns toward the subdued display; human figure appears after
      this line
    completionEvent: audio_complete
    sequence: 3
    segments:
    - Then watching from out here won't help.
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: e5e84d5cd2a7ee8478a3a884ad01fded, type: 3}
  - id: S02_L04
    scene: Scene02
    speaker: Niko
    type: Core
    layer: StoryboardCore
    text: We need to go inside somewhere humans can't.
    filename: 04_we_need_to_go
    visualCue: 'Wide: Niko and the revealed human'
    completionEvent: audio_complete
    sequence: 4
    segments:
    - We need to go inside somewhere humans can't.
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 15580d9244c53d74a9691b898f436bd3, type: 3}
  - id: S02_L05
    scene: Scene02
    speaker: Niko
    type: PromptVO
    layer: StoryboardCore
    text: Click on the SCAN button.
    filename: 05_click_on_the_scan
    visualCue: Niko raises his hand; SCAN button pulses
    completionEvent: audio_complete_then_scan_pressed
    sequence: 5
    segments:
    - Click on the SCAN button.
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 1e7f33e59c3b46b48b9b1d76dbc542bc, type: 3}
  - id: S02_L06
    scene: Scene02
    speaker: Niko
    type: Core
    layer: StoryboardCore
    text: There.
    filename: 06_there
    visualCue: One eye illuminates as the line starts
    completionEvent: audio_complete
    sequence: 6
    segments:
    - There.
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 63ea1327f84b1c348b461425dbcca5f6, type: 3}
  - id: S02_L07
    scene: Scene02
    speaker: Niko
    type: Core
    layer: StoryboardCore
    text: Your first destination.
    filename: 07_your_first_destination
    visualCue: Anatomical close-up of the eye inside the skull
    completionEvent: audio_complete
    sequence: 7
    segments:
    - Your first destination.
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 4d83305a78efa90479e12a788f0391b7, type: 3}
  - id: S02_L08
    scene: Scene02
    speaker: Niko
    type: Core
    layer: StoryboardCore
    text: Here it is. The human eye.
    filename: 08_here_it_is_the
    visualCue: Enlarged eye in front of learner, slow rotation
    completionEvent: audio_complete
    sequence: 8
    segments:
    - Here it is. The human eye.
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 755efec1a067b354eaf3d213eb5a5a5f, type: 3}
  - id: S02_L09
    scene: Scene02
    speaker: Niko
    type: Core
    layer: StoryboardCore
    text: It has several parts, and each one has an important job.
    filename: 09_it_has_several_parts
    visualCue: Niko gestures toward the eye
    completionEvent: audio_complete
    sequence: 9
    segments:
    - It has several parts, and each one has an important job.
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: a2db006b7867dea44ae315268f7dc2d1, type: 3}
  - id: S02_L10
    scene: Scene02
    speaker: Niko
    type: Core
    layer: StoryboardCore
    text: Click or ask Niko about each part to explore what it does.
    filename: 10_click_or_ask_niko
    visualCue: 'After Niko''s snap: sclera, cornea, iris, pupil highlight in turn'
    completionEvent: audio_complete_then_exploration
    sequence: 10
    segments:
    - Click or ask Niko about each part to explore what it does.
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 8a9f66426e1ccab4ca9f5700e7ab26e4, type: 3}
  - id: S02_L11
    scene: Scene02
    speaker: Niko
    type: Core
    layer: StoryboardCore
    text: This tough white outer layer is called the sclera. It protects the eye
      and helps maintain its shape.
    filename: 11_this_tough_white_outer
    visualCue: Close-up of sclera; other parts translucent
    completionEvent: audio_complete_marks_part
    sequence: 11
    segments:
    - This tough white outer layer is called the sclera.
    - It protects the eye and helps maintain its shape.
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 315719b89b736a741a31c097d93b8537, type: 3}
  - id: S02_L12
    scene: Scene02
    speaker: Niko
    type: Core
    layer: StoryboardCore
    text: This transparent, curved layer at the front is the cornea. It protects
      the eye and bends incoming light.
    filename: 12_this_transparent_curved_layer
    visualCue: Close-up of cornea profile; other parts translucent
    completionEvent: audio_complete_marks_part
    sequence: 12
    segments:
    - This transparent, curved layer at the front is the cornea.
    - It protects the eye and bends incoming light.
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: d0bc35cea4e994c4e853ba49daca356f, type: 3}
  - id: S02_L13
    scene: Scene02
    speaker: Niko
    type: Core
    layer: StoryboardCore
    text: This coloured part is the iris. It controls the size of the pupil.
    filename: 13_this_coloured_part_is
    visualCue: Front close-up of iris; other parts translucent
    completionEvent: audio_complete_marks_part
    sequence: 13
    segments:
    - This coloured part is the iris. It controls the size of the pupil.
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 6bd775bc91a044c4284246dfa157e643, type: 3}
  - id: S02_L14
    scene: Scene02
    speaker: Niko
    type: Core
    layer: StoryboardCore
    text: This opening is the pupil. Light enters the eye through it.
    filename: 14_this_opening_is_the
    visualCue: Pupil rim highlighted as an opening; camera pulls back
    completionEvent: audio_complete_marks_part
    sequence: 14
    segments:
    - This opening is the pupil. Light enters the eye through it.
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 7ab995c7baee58d45a8c3005c33bb631, type: 3}
  - id: S02_L15
    scene: Scene02
    speaker: Niko
    type: Core
    layer: StoryboardCore
    text: "We\u2019ve seen the parts we can see from the outside. Now, let\u2019s
      look inside."
    filename: 15_weve_seen_the_parts
    visualCue: Complete eye; Niko gestures
    completionEvent: audio_complete
    sequence: 15
    segments:
    - "We\u2019ve seen the parts we can see from the outside. Now, let\u2019s look
      inside."
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 4fd5701285d6655428c0d9c9f7003708, type: 3}
  - id: S02_L16
    scene: Scene02
    speaker: Niko
    type: PromptVO
    layer: StoryboardCore
    text: Click on the Inside View button to see how the eye looks from the inside.
    filename: 16_click_on_the_inside
    visualCue: Inside View button enabled
    completionEvent: audio_complete_then_inside_pressed
    sequence: 16
    segments:
    - Click on the Inside View button to see how the eye looks from the inside.
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 27d60203378100840b7a5a95d4a7cda9, type: 3}
  - id: S03_L01
    scene: Scene03
    speaker: Niko
    type: Core
    layer: StoryboardCore
    text: Click or ask Niko about each part to explore what it does.
    filename: 17_click_or_ask_niko
    visualCue: Cutaway eye; internal parts highlight in turn
    completionEvent: audio_complete_then_exploration
    sequence: 17
    segments:
    - Click or ask Niko about each part to explore what it does.
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 7cc62b3a95e59d549aa4b39f84d5b265, type: 3}
  - id: S03_L02
    scene: Scene03
    speaker: Niko
    type: Core
    layer: StoryboardCore
    text: This space between the cornea and the lens contains a clear fluid called
      aqueous humour.
    filename: 18_this_space_between_the
    visualCue: Aqueous region highlighted, camera closer
    completionEvent: audio_complete
    sequence: 18
    segments:
    - This space between the cornea and the lens contains a clear fluid called aqueous
      humour.
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 64eff01135a836a46928bf83019bcbef, type: 3}
  - id: S03_L03
    scene: Scene03
    speaker: Niko
    type: Core
    layer: StoryboardCore
    text: It helps nourish the front parts of the eye and helps maintain pressure
      inside the eye.
    filename: 19_it_helps_nourish_the
    visualCue: Hold on aqueous region
    completionEvent: audio_complete_marks_part
    sequence: 19
    segments:
    - It helps nourish the front parts of the eye and helps maintain pressure inside
      the eye.
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: f6b3e0c6c69d6484380503bcaf1d7417, type: 3}
  - id: S03_L04
    scene: Scene03
    speaker: Niko
    type: Core
    layer: StoryboardCore
    text: "Behind the pupil is the eye\u2019s natural crystalline lens."
    filename: 20_behind_the_pupil_is
    visualCue: Lens highlighted, camera closer
    completionEvent: audio_complete
    sequence: 20
    segments:
    - "Behind the pupil is the eye\u2019s natural crystalline lens."
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: dd130078ba0959f40917f5cc9b193eab, type: 3}
  - id: S03_L05
    scene: Scene03
    speaker: Niko
    type: Core
    layer: StoryboardCore
    text: It is transparent, flexible and biconvex, meaning it bulges outward on
      both sides.
    filename: 21_it_is_transparent_flexible
    visualCue: Lens close-up, biconvex profile
    completionEvent: audio_complete
    sequence: 21
    segments:
    - It is transparent, flexible and biconvex, meaning it bulges outward on both
      sides.
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 0aca7d40f0ff627449880dfbd92dbaae, type: 3}
  - id: S03_L06
    scene: Scene03
    speaker: Niko
    type: Core
    layer: StoryboardCore
    text: It can change its shape to help focus light from objects at different distances.
    filename: 22_it_can_change_its
    visualCue: Lens changes shape slightly; view widens
    completionEvent: audio_complete_marks_part
    sequence: 22
    segments:
    - It can change its shape to help focus light from objects at different distances.
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 9a61475dbcef4374f9f5d38349f9ad42, type: 3}
  - id: S03_L07
    scene: Scene03
    speaker: Niko
    type: Core
    layer: StoryboardCore
    text: Most of the space behind the lens is filled with a clear, jelly-like substance
      called vitreous humour.
    filename: 23_most_of_the_space
    visualCue: Camera moves through vitreous toward the back
    completionEvent: audio_complete
    sequence: 23
    segments:
    - Most of the space behind the lens is filled with a clear, jelly-like substance
      called vitreous humour.
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 5f9a662e6c8736b45a3e50fed148b36c, type: 3}
  - id: S03_L08
    scene: Scene03
    speaker: Niko
    type: Core
    layer: StoryboardCore
    text: It helps maintain the shape of the eye.
    filename: 24_it_helps_maintain_the
    visualCue: Hold on vitreous region
    completionEvent: audio_complete_marks_part
    sequence: 24
    segments:
    - It helps maintain the shape of the eye.
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: b256a837aac61514b8aa92be993373e7, type: 3}
  - id: S03_L09
    scene: Scene03
    speaker: Niko
    type: Core
    layer: StoryboardCore
    text: This inner layer at the back is the retina.
    filename: 25_this_inner_layer_at
    visualCue: Camera very close to retinal surface
    completionEvent: audio_complete
    sequence: 25
    segments:
    - This inner layer at the back is the retina.
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 965cae2aa34b69c4d8737dac1e9273dd, type: 3}
  - id: S03_L10
    scene: Scene03
    speaker: Niko
    type: Core
    layer: StoryboardCore
    text: It contains light-sensitive cells that detect light.
    filename: 26_it_contains_lightsensitive_cells
    visualCue: Retinal detail; camera moves slightly deeper
    completionEvent: audio_complete_marks_part
    sequence: 26
    segments:
    - It contains light-sensitive cells that detect light.
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: a1604c91f9ddd5f4f866573171c8950a, type: 3}
  - id: S03_L11
    scene: Scene03
    speaker: Niko
    type: Core
    layer: StoryboardCore
    text: Behind the retina is the choroid, a layer rich in blood vessels that supplies
      the eye with oxygen and nutrients.
    filename: 27_behind_the_retina_is
    visualCue: Choroid highlighted behind retina
    completionEvent: audio_complete_marks_part
    sequence: 27
    segments:
    - Behind the retina is the choroid, a layer rich in blood vessels that supplies
      the eye with oxygen and nutrients.
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 8eb1bab8349158543b7c4d09e701c417, type: 3}
  - id: S03_L12
    scene: Scene03
    speaker: Niko
    type: Core
    layer: StoryboardCore
    text: "Now we\u2019ve explored the main structures of the eye."
    filename: 28_now_weve_explored_the
    visualCue: Complete cutaway eye
    completionEvent: audio_complete
    sequence: 28
    segments:
    - "Now we\u2019ve explored the main structures of the eye."
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 7fa24aa74f84a0d4591727b8ebf76f17, type: 3}
  - id: S04_L01
    scene: Scene04
    speaker: Niko
    type: Core
    layer: StoryboardCore
    text: "But there\u2019s something important we haven\u2019t explored yet."
    filename: 29_but_theres_something_important
    visualCue: Camera begins moving toward the back of the eye
    completionEvent: audio_complete
    sequence: 29
    segments:
    - "But there\u2019s something important we haven\u2019t explored yet."
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: c7a9f7c5f4ecfe84c8e8593ad911b444, type: 3}
  - id: S04_L02
    scene: Scene04
    speaker: Niko
    type: Core
    layer: StoryboardCore
    text: "We know that the retina detects light\u2026"
    filename: 30_we_know_that_the
    visualCue: Back of the eye comes closer
    completionEvent: audio_complete
    sequence: 30
    segments:
    - "We know that the retina detects light\u2026"
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 0bb465d724300d840946e6fa538b03dd, type: 3}
  - id: S04_L03
    scene: Scene04
    speaker: Niko
    type: Core
    layer: StoryboardCore
    text: "\u2026but how does that information reach the brain?"
    filename: 31_but_how_does_that
    visualCue: Nerve bundle extends into view
    completionEvent: audio_complete
    sequence: 31
    segments:
    - "\u2026but how does that information reach the brain?"
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: ceee4240fe5a79d4fb8edd6204bf72ed, type: 3}
  - id: S04_L04
    scene: Scene04
    speaker: Niko
    type: Core
    layer: StoryboardCore
    text: "Let\u2019s follow it."
    filename: 32_lets_follow_it
    visualCue: Bundle highlighted
    completionEvent: audio_complete
    sequence: 32
    segments:
    - "Let\u2019s follow it."
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 24fe602a7d551d145a1680fc351427d6, type: 3}
  - id: S04_L05
    scene: Scene04
    speaker: Niko
    type: Core
    layer: StoryboardCore
    text: This bundle is the optic nerve.
    filename: 33_this_bundle_is_the
    visualCue: Close on optic nerve leaving the eye
    completionEvent: audio_complete
    sequence: 33
    segments:
    - This bundle is the optic nerve.
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: bf851f27cf7094042ba6f091fa4be261, type: 3}
  - id: S04_L06
    scene: Scene04
    speaker: Niko
    type: Core
    layer: StoryboardCore
    text: It carries visual information from the retina to the brain.
    filename: 34_it_carries_visual_information
    visualCue: Camera follows nerve toward the brain
    completionEvent: audio_complete
    sequence: 34
    segments:
    - It carries visual information from the retina to the brain.
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 23eaf21420d050e4785a23ae0b550a29, type: 3}
  - id: S04_L07
    scene: Scene04
    speaker: Niko
    type: Core
    layer: StoryboardCore
    text: The brain receives and processes this information so that we can see.
    filename: 35_the_brain_receives_and
    visualCue: Visual processing area at back of brain highlighted
    completionEvent: audio_complete
    sequence: 35
    segments:
    - The brain receives and processes this information so that we can see.
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 555b9b5d5c087d04090e28f59cf1de46, type: 3}
  - id: S04_L08
    scene: Scene04
    speaker: Niko
    type: Core
    layer: StoryboardCore
    text: So the eye and brain are connected through the optic nerve.
    filename: 36_so_the_eye_and
    visualCue: 'Wide: eye, optic nerve and brain together'
    completionEvent: audio_complete
    sequence: 36
    segments:
    - So the eye and brain are connected through the optic nerve.
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 18eb4e0cc3d787f419e2e643fb612301, type: 3}
  - id: S05_L01
    scene: Scene05
    speaker: Niko
    type: Core
    layer: StoryboardCore
    text: "We've been looking at the eye. Now let\u2019s follow what happens when
      you look at an object."
    filename: 37_weve_been_looking_at
    visualCue: Illuminated apple and eye
    completionEvent: audio_complete
    sequence: 37
    segments:
    - "We've been looking at the eye. Now let\u2019s follow what happens when you
      look at an object."
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: efff87e412d864146b161c894592fc98, type: 3}
  - id: S05_L02
    scene: Scene05
    speaker: Niko
    type: Core
    layer: StoryboardCore
    text: Vision begins when light from an object reaches the eye.
    filename: 38_vision_begins_when_light
    visualCue: Light travels from the object to the eye
    completionEvent: audio_complete
    sequence: 38
    segments:
    - Vision begins when light from an object reaches the eye.
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 8fb69821a504b434d81d1667498d8c50, type: 3}
  - id: S05_L03
    scene: Scene05
    speaker: Niko
    type: Core
    layer: StoryboardCore
    text: First, the light passes through the cornea, which bends it.
    filename: 39_first_the_light_passes
    visualCue: Rays bend at the cornea
    completionEvent: audio_complete
    sequence: 39
    segments:
    - First, the light passes through the cornea, which bends it.
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 5160ff69607d6524bae168538f91284d, type: 3}
  - id: S05_L04
    scene: Scene05
    speaker: Niko
    type: Core
    layer: StoryboardCore
    text: It then travels through the aqueous humour and enters through the pupil.
    filename: 40_it_then_travels_through
    visualCue: Rays through aqueous and pupil
    completionEvent: audio_complete
    sequence: 40
    segments:
    - It then travels through the aqueous humour and enters through the pupil.
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 4611a60adfb9a2f4f96c0ad3758d7566, type: 3}
  - id: S05_L05
    scene: Scene05
    speaker: Niko
    type: PromptVO
    layer: StoryboardCore
    text: Change the brightness and observe what happens to the pupil.
    filename: 41_change_the_brightness_and
    visualCue: Brightness controls enabled
    completionEvent: audio_complete_then_brightness
    sequence: 41
    segments:
    - Change the brightness and observe what happens to the pupil.
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: df33e6743ea993f478c4b886b4f7613c, type: 3}
  - id: S05_L06
    scene: Scene05
    speaker: Niko
    type: Core
    layer: StoryboardCore
    text: In bright light, the pupil becomes smaller.
    filename: 42_in_bright_light_the
    visualCue: Pupil has constricted
    completionEvent: audio_complete
    sequence: 42
    segments:
    - In bright light, the pupil becomes smaller.
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 5e4ffdbb8d00f1b47a06c78e671ae6db, type: 3}
  - id: S05_L07
    scene: Scene05
    speaker: Niko
    type: Core
    layer: StoryboardCore
    text: In dimmer light, the pupil becomes larger.
    filename: 43_in_dimmer_light_the
    visualCue: Pupil has dilated
    completionEvent: audio_complete
    sequence: 43
    segments:
    - In dimmer light, the pupil becomes larger.
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: fe6298f4509cf3343a92c25f2644b9fe, type: 3}
  - id: S05_L08
    scene: Scene05
    speaker: Niko
    type: Core
    layer: StoryboardCore
    text: The iris controls the size of the pupil and therefore regulates how much
      light enters the eye.
    filename: 44_the_iris_controls_the
    visualCue: Iris highlighted
    completionEvent: audio_complete
    sequence: 44
    segments:
    - The iris controls the size of the pupil and therefore regulates how much light
      enters the eye.
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 10857f1a52615374db4c6eede6a8fd85, type: 3}
  - id: S06_L01
    scene: Scene06
    speaker: Niko
    type: Core
    layer: StoryboardCore
    text: "After passing through the pupil, the light reaches the eye\u2019s crystalline
      lens."
    filename: 45_after_passing_through_the
    visualCue: Lens close-up; rays bend through lens
    completionEvent: audio_complete
    sequence: 45
    segments:
    - "After passing through the pupil, the light reaches the eye\u2019s crystalline
      lens."
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: c29474ff176651a4199bff2202cefac8, type: 3}
  - id: S06_L02
    scene: Scene06
    speaker: Niko
    type: Core
    layer: StoryboardCore
    text: For a nearby object, the lens becomes more curved so that the light can
      be focused correctly.
    filename: 46_for_a_nearby_object
    visualCue: Near object; lens more curved
    completionEvent: audio_complete
    sequence: 46
    segments:
    - For a nearby object, the lens becomes more curved so that the light can be
      focused correctly.
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 631cb05472e88684da7ac8dcb7fadf53, type: 3}
  - id: S06_L03
    scene: Scene06
    speaker: Niko
    type: Core
    layer: StoryboardCore
    text: For a distant object, the lens becomes less curved.
    filename: 47_for_a_distant_object
    visualCue: Distant object; lens less curved
    completionEvent: audio_complete
    sequence: 47
    segments:
    - For a distant object, the lens becomes less curved.
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 7e4e2d23fdb6c5244a8f4f767d410493, type: 3}
  - id: S06_L04
    scene: Scene06
    speaker: Niko
    type: Core
    layer: StoryboardCore
    text: This continuous adjustment of the lens to focus objects at different distances
      is called accommodation.
    filename: 48_this_continuous_adjustment_of
    visualCue: 'Pull back: light continues through vitreous'
    completionEvent: audio_complete
    sequence: 48
    segments:
    - This continuous adjustment of the lens to focus objects at different distances
      is called accommodation.
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 914b69f688a874146ab47343638be1b0, type: 3}
  - id: S07_L01
    scene: Scene07
    speaker: Niko
    type: Core
    layer: StoryboardCore
    text: After passing through the lens and vitreous humour, the light reaches the
      retina.
    filename: 49_after_passing_through_the
    visualCue: Rays converge on the retina
    completionEvent: audio_complete
    sequence: 49
    segments:
    - After passing through the lens and vitreous humour, the light reaches the retina.
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: e2dcda053a119994d8c5f28d29528cce, type: 3}
  - id: S07_L02
    scene: Scene07
    speaker: Niko
    type: Core
    layer: StoryboardCore
    text: The lens forms a real, inverted image of the object on the retina.
    filename: 50_the_lens_forms_a
    visualCue: Inverted retinal image shown clearly
    completionEvent: audio_complete
    sequence: 50
    segments:
    - The lens forms a real, inverted image of the object on the retina.
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 05030038414efee498a2c31b1daef787, type: 3}
  - id: S07_L03
    scene: Scene07
    speaker: Niko
    type: Core
    layer: StoryboardCore
    text: But what exactly detects this light on the retina?
    filename: 51_but_what_exactly_detects
    visualCue: Camera closer to retinal surface
    completionEvent: audio_complete
    sequence: 51
    segments:
    - But what exactly detects this light on the retina?
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: b44e702c16731bd48a3f65b317791aa6, type: 3}
  - id: S08_L01
    scene: Scene08
    speaker: Niko
    type: Core
    layer: StoryboardCore
    text: The retina contains light-sensitive cells called photoreceptors.
    filename: 52_the_retina_contains_lightsensitive
    visualCue: Magnified retina; photoreceptors visible
    completionEvent: audio_complete
    sequence: 52
    segments:
    - The retina contains light-sensitive cells called photoreceptors.
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: fe65e8f8f30eae5499e3d03d61a4ad1f, type: 3}
  - id: S08_L02
    scene: Scene08
    speaker: Niko
    type: Core
    layer: StoryboardCore
    text: Rods are especially sensitive to low levels of light and help us see in
      dim conditions.
    filename: 53_rods_are_especially_sensitive
    visualCue: Rods highlighted
    completionEvent: audio_complete
    sequence: 53
    segments:
    - Rods are especially sensitive to low levels of light and help us see in dim
      conditions.
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: c3d234f7d04af0f4d88ea9b08d59a671, type: 3}
  - id: S08_L03
    scene: Scene08
    speaker: Niko
    type: Core
    layer: StoryboardCore
    text: They mainly provide information about brightness rather than colour.
    filename: 54_they_mainly_provide_information
    visualCue: Rods remain highlighted
    completionEvent: audio_complete
    sequence: 54
    segments:
    - They mainly provide information about brightness rather than colour.
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 5f536cd0d2cdb4b48977cade2090f950, type: 3}
  - id: S08_L04
    scene: Scene08
    speaker: Niko
    type: Core
    layer: StoryboardCore
    text: Cones work best in brighter light and allow us to see colours and fine
      details.
    filename: 55_cones_work_best_in
    visualCue: Cones highlighted
    completionEvent: audio_complete
    sequence: 55
    segments:
    - Cones work best in brighter light and allow us to see colours and fine details.
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 98b8d10e677c3e7498b19f53e94c7087, type: 3}
  - id: S08_L05
    scene: Scene08
    speaker: Niko
    type: Core
    layer: StoryboardCore
    text: When light reaches these cells, it is converted into electrical signals.
    filename: 56_when_light_reaches_these
    visualCue: Light reaches cells; electrical response
    completionEvent: audio_complete
    sequence: 56
    segments:
    - When light reaches these cells, it is converted into electrical signals.
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 41e14330e6e5b4141b3e8b2245245a2b, type: 3}
  - id: S08_L06
    scene: Scene08
    speaker: Niko
    type: Core
    layer: StoryboardCore
    text: These signals are passed through the retina toward the optic nerve.
    filename: 57_these_signals_are_passed
    visualCue: Signals pass through retinal cells toward optic nerve
    completionEvent: audio_complete
    sequence: 57
    segments:
    - These signals are passed through the retina toward the optic nerve.
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 91056e8ea3c863b4284e3a54bdf5a949, type: 3}
  - id: S09_L01
    scene: Scene09
    speaker: Niko
    type: Core
    layer: StoryboardCore
    text: The electrical signals leave the eye through the optic nerve.
    filename: 58_the_electrical_signals_leave
    visualCue: Signals leave retina into optic nerve
    completionEvent: audio_complete
    sequence: 58
    segments:
    - The electrical signals leave the eye through the optic nerve.
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: c2b725e855bc8b249a6148c9281aa013, type: 3}
  - id: S09_L02
    scene: Scene09
    speaker: Niko
    type: Core
    layer: StoryboardCore
    text: The optic nerve carries this visual information to the brain.
    filename: 59_the_optic_nerve_carries
    visualCue: Camera follows nerve to brain
    completionEvent: audio_complete
    sequence: 59
    segments:
    - The optic nerve carries this visual information to the brain.
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: fd4613986a1f48c4aafd83565f76a2fc, type: 3}
  - id: S09_L03
    scene: Scene09
    speaker: Niko
    type: Core
    layer: StoryboardCore
    text: The brain receives and processes these signals to produce our visual perception.
    filename: 60_the_brain_receives_and
    visualCue: Visual processing area highlighted
    completionEvent: audio_complete
    sequence: 60
    segments:
    - The brain receives and processes these signals to produce our visual perception.
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 028cde1c5bb5ead4db12ddafb2a6820c, type: 3}
  - id: S09_L04
    scene: Scene09
    speaker: Niko
    type: Core
    layer: StoryboardCore
    text: Although the image formed on the retina is inverted, our visual experience
      is not simply a photograph of that retinal image. The brain processes the information
      carried by the signals.
    filename: 61_although_the_image_formed
    visualCue: Original object shown clearly; retinal image and perception as separate
      views
    completionEvent: audio_complete
    sequence: 61
    segments:
    - Although the image formed on the retina is inverted, our visual experience
      is not simply a photograph of that retinal image.
    - The brain processes the information carried by the signals.
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 095651d2bf40a0f48a2acca835af4f0f, type: 3}
  - id: S10_L01
    scene: Scene10
    speaker: Niko
    type: Core
    layer: StoryboardCore
    text: So seeing is a complete process.
    filename: 62_so_seeing_is_a
    visualCue: Pull back to complete eye
    completionEvent: audio_complete
    sequence: 62
    segments:
    - So seeing is a complete process.
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: b0ff1dcebf1018344922166073b28522, type: 3}
  - id: S10_L02
    scene: Scene10
    speaker: Niko
    type: Core
    layer: StoryboardCore
    text: "Now you\u2019ve followed the journey from the moment light enters the
      eye to the moment the brain processes the information."
    filename: 63_now_youve_followed_the
    visualCue: Complete eye, nerve and brain
    completionEvent: audio_complete
    sequence: 63
    segments:
    - "Now you\u2019ve followed the journey from the moment light enters the eye
      to the moment the brain processes the information."
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 02a26d53df90f23429ffc6e9c27fc461, type: 3}
  - id: S11_L01
    scene: Scene11
    speaker: Niko
    type: Core
    layer: StoryboardCore
    text: "Your eyes are constantly responding to the world around you\u2014even
      when you\u2019re not thinking about it."
    filename: 64_your_eyes_are_constantly
    visualCue: Complete eye
    completionEvent: audio_complete
    sequence: 64
    segments:
    - "Your eyes are constantly responding to the world around you\u2014even when
      you\u2019re not thinking about it."
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 23e8f2cc9868f6f478fa6fbfbb0eabb4, type: 3}
  - id: S11_L02
    scene: Scene11
    speaker: Niko
    type: Core
    layer: StoryboardCore
    text: "So here\u2019s something to think about\u2026what happens when the eye
      cannot focus light properly?"
    filename: 65_so_heres_something_to
    visualCue: Then distant object slightly blurred, near object clear
    completionEvent: audio_complete
    sequence: 65
    segments:
    - "So here\u2019s something to think about\u2026what happens when the eye cannot
      focus light properly?"
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 6dd30bb9149d95b4bbc4b6e6b2b95ac8, type: 3}
  - id: S11_L03
    scene: Scene11
    speaker: Niko
    type: Core
    layer: StoryboardCore
    text: Why might some things look blurry, even when your eyes are working?
    filename: 66_why_might_some_things
    visualCue: Blurred object fades; eye fades; cut to black
    completionEvent: audio_complete
    sequence: 66
    segments:
    - Why might some things look blurry, even when your eyes are working?
    clip: {fileID: 8300000, guid: 538c67788711af340aa0edaa657ac5a2, type: 3}
